url: "https://github.com/MohitGoyal09/following-the-checker"
abstract: >-
  Community Notes checks whether a note looks sourced, not whether the cited page
  supports the claim. We test how three chat LLMs (Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Haiku 5.5,
  Gemini 3.8 Flash) use a source-check verdict that can be wrong, with and without the
  passage the checker read, on 80 real Helpful notes (1,920 answers), and we check at
  the page level whether the links in 200 paired AI-written and human-written Helpful
  notes support their claims. Code, data, preregistration and report from the Apart
  Research AI x Epistemics Research Sprint, November 2026.
keywords:
